// The spall cone's shape and its potency — the field thrown from every body exit a round
// reaches —, and a burst's field. Read by `src/ballistics/spall_cone.rs`, embedded and parsed once,
// validated at parse.
// The law itself (strength, the ball law's centre-weighted profile, shadowing, dose) is design doc
// §5, `.agents/docs/design/armor-penetration-and-damage.md`; this file holds its shape data and the
// share of the energy its round lost that a cone's strength is. A field's strength and every one of
// its deposits are joules, and turn into HP points at the one energy-to-HP rate every dose converts
// at (`assets/ballistics/energy_dose.ron`). A cone's half-angle and profile are not here: both
// follow from its field's ratio, the exit layer's substance's (`debris_half_angle_deg` in
// `assets/materials/materials.ron`).
//
// Every value here is a choice the owner can change by editing this file alone; none is a
// constant of the law. The playtest fork on the axis is F5 in
// `.agents/scratch/playtest-forks/README.md`.
//
// PROVENANCE: every value is authored `(value, Kind("source or reason"))`, Kind one of Measured,
// Derived, Tuned, Resolution, Unknown (`src/provenance.rs`); a value without one does not load.
(
    // The cone's axis. `RearNormalBisector`: normalize(rear-face outward normal + exit direction)
    // at a genuine exit, the exit direction at an internal step (which has no face).
    // `ExitDirection`: the exit direction everywhere.
    axis: (RearNormalBisector, Tuned("engineering assumption (playtest fork F5) with MEASURED
        support: debris axis about halfway between the shot line and the plate normal, 25°
        measured against 22.5° predicted at 45° obliquity (Verolme 1997, Recht & Howell 1967;
        research/cloud-angle-deep.md)")),

    // N, the number of directions the cone is sampled by, in equal-solid-angle strata of 1/N of the
    // cone each, every one weighted by its stratum's share of the field. The emitted total is S/2
    // at every N, so N changes how finely a box's dose is resolved, never how much the cone
    // carries.
    directions: (64, Tuned("owner decision 2026-10-17 ('64 for now'), the cost against the
        resolution: one throw under the ball law MEASURED 2026-10-24 by
        ballistics::pen_cam::spall_law_cost (release, macOS arm64, best of 9, the 7 cones of the
        penetrating scenarios): 0.30 ms at N = 24, 0.64 at 64, 1.23 at 128, 2.29 at 256; the dose
        step per direction on the s1 cone at 64 runs from 10.5 HP on the axis to 0.65 HP at the
        rim, 6.25 HP on average (DERIVED: S·f_k / 3000 J per HP / 64, S = 2.40 MJ MEASURED from
        the s1 record). The count changes how finely a box's dose is resolved, never the emitted
        total")),

    // The cone's strength S (J) per joule of the kinetic energy its round lost across the body it
    // left, ½ m (v_entry² − v_exit²), m the mass that meets the plate (a sub-calibre round's core):
    // the energy the line's dose is (`energy_dose.ron`). The cone emits S/2 in all, and its
    // deposits convert at that file's rate. It sets the potency of every cone at once and nothing
    // else: the shape and the field law both conserve a cone's emitted total.
    energy_share: (0.88, Tuned("provisional (issue 116, owner decision 2026-10-28: the simplest
        model): set so that the reference case throws a cone of the strength the retired law
        (spend × κ × (v_exit / v_entry)² × (d / 88 mm)², converting at 70 HP points per
        reference-mm) gave it. The reference case: the reference 88 mm APCBC round (10.2 kg, nose
        factor 7/24) at its 773 m/s muzzle speed perforating its reference plate, 100 mm of
        reference steel at normal impact (ASSUMED: the plate the retired rate was set against,
        the s1 cone's, is 101 mm at 10.9°). DERIVED from the force law: the round reads 114.93
        reference-mm at 773 m/s and leaves the plate at 259.69 m/s; the retired law's S was
        100 × (259.69 / 773)² = 11.286 reference-mm, emitting 395.0 HP points; the round loses
        ½ × 10.2 × (773² − 259.69²) = 2.7035 MJ; a cone emitting 395.0 HP points at 3000 J per HP
        has S = 2.3701 MJ, so the share is 2.3701 / 2.7035 = 0.877, rounded to 0.88 (the reference
        cone emits 396.5 HP points, +0.4 %). Its knockout radius for the 30 HP crew pool at a
        0.2 m² mean face through RHA (α = 26.2°, Ω_c = 0.646 sr) is 2.02 m at an average spot and
        2.63 m on the axis (DERIVED: R = sqrt(2 f(θ) E A / (pool Ω_c)), E = S/2 in HP points,
        f = ½ and 0.842). A round loses more energy through a thicker plate, so a barely
        perforating round throws the strongest cone of a plate and a thin plate a weak one")),

    // A burst's field (design doc §5a, "The burst"): thrown from the burst point about the round's
    // flight direction, its ratio the carried speed over the burst's greatest sideways speed v_s,
    // through the struck tank's volumes, passing as the spall cone's directions do, its deposits
    // converting at `energy_dose.ron`'s rate. Every burst is a ring: the wall around the burst
    // core is driven as a band about the flight axis, and the nose piece flies on.
    burst: (
        // The burst's strength S (J) per joule of its own driven energy: the kinetic energy its
        // explosive gives the wall, ½ M v_s², M the wall and v_s the greatest sideways speed, DERIVED
        // per round at load (`Burst::energy`, `src/ballistics/burst.rs`). The field carries that
        // energy times this factor and emits S/2 in all; nothing the round lost reaching the burst
        // point enters it, since a burst's energy comes from its explosive. At 1 the field would
        // carry its driven energy and nothing more; the factor that keeps every shipped burst as
        // strong as it was is far from 1.
        driven_energy_factor: (210.0, Tuned("provisional, flagged for the owner: the burst's
            potency set against an HP target, not against the energy its wall carries, so the
            factor is far above 1: the ring emits 105 times its driven energy. DERIVED to keep
            every burst's potency: 1.0 reference-mm per kJ of driven energy at 70 HP points per
            reference-mm is 0.07 HP points per J, × 3000 J per HP = 210 J of strength per J
            driven, the same HP from every burst. That rate was set
            against an even sphere at rest, the burst's ball until playtest fork F7 retired it: a
            crew box presenting a 0.2 m² face (a seated crew member's) fully inside it, 2.0 m from
            the burst, has its 30 HP pool emptied. DERIVED: the box catches A/(4πR²) of the
            emission E = S/2, and its knockout radius is R = sqrt(E A / (30 × 4π)), E in HP
            points; R = 2.0 m needs E = 7540 HP points against the 214.8 kJ that ball drove (the
            8.8 cm Pzgr. 39 less its core). The ring at rest is 5.76 times as bright in its band,
            R = 4.75 m (design doc §5a, DERIVED). A field that carried only its driven energy
            (factor 2, emitting ½ M v_s²) would emit 132.6 HP points from the shipped ring's
            397.7 kJ against 13,922 at 210 (DERIVED), a knockout radius 10.2 times shorter")),
        // h (degrees): the ring spans θ_c − h to θ_c + h of polar angle from the flight axis,
        // θ_c = atan(1/λ), uniform over that band; its near edge is held at the axis.
        ring_half_width_deg: (10.0, Tuned("provisional (owner's brief 4b): the band the wall's
            fragments leave in, one datum for every ring")),
        // N for the ring, as `directions` is for the cone: the emitted total is S/2 at every N, so
        // N sets how finely a box's dose is resolved, never how much the burst carries. One
        // throw's cost MEASURED 2026-10-24 by ballistics::pen_cam::burst_law_cost (release, macOS
        // arm64, best of 9, s1's line fired with the burst round). At rest each direction carries
        // S/2 / N joules, S/2 / (3000 N) HP points of dose (DERIVED, the field uniform over its
        // support).
        ring_directions: (256, Tuned("provisional, flagged for the owner: the cost against the
            resolution. The ring's throw: 0.50 ms at N = 64, 1.47 at 256, 4.01 at 684; at rest
            218, 54 and 20 HP points per direction (S = 210 × 397.7 kJ = 83.53 MJ), so at 256 one
            direction is about two crew pools")),
    ),
)
